<p>In Claude Code:</p>
<pre>claude mcp add --transport http --scope user modelfy https://mcp-dev.modelfy.ai/mcp</pre>
<p>Chat assistants (claude.ai, Claude Desktop, ChatGPT) sign in with your Modelfy account once. Coding agents and bots can use an API key in the <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> header. Every client, step by step: <a href="/docs/connect">Connect your agent</a>.</p>

<h2>Get a key</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Try it now, no account:</strong> <code>curl -X POST https://mcp-dev.modelfy.ai/sandbox/keys</code> gives a free sandbox key. Nothing is spent; photos are samples.</li>
<li><strong>Device login:</strong> <code>POST https://mcp-dev.modelfy.ai/device/code</code>, open the link it returns, approve, then poll <code>POST https://mcp-dev.modelfy.ai/device/token</code>. The key comes to your agent; nobody copies it.</li>
<li><strong>By hand:</strong> create a key in your Modelfy account and paste it.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Spending</h2>
<p>Every session is planned first with its exact price (<code>plan_photos</code>). In a chat the person confirms it; a live API key spends only within the credit budget its owner set.</p>

